# Bandit Level 13 → 14
## Goal
Use the provided SSH private key to log in as `bandit14` and obtain the password.
## Steps
On Bandit Level 13:
```bash
ls
cat sshkey.private
```
Copy the complete private key, including:
```text
-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----
...
-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----
```
Exit the Bandit server:
```bash
exit
```
On your local terminal, create a file:
```bash
nano bandit14.key
```
Paste the private key and save it. Then set the correct permissions:
```bash
chmod 600 bandit14.key
```
Connect using the private key:
```bash
ssh -i bandit14.key bandit14@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220
```
After successfully logging in:
```bash
cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit14
```
This displays the password for Bandit Level 14.
## Key Learning
This level introduces **SSH key-based authentication**. Instead of using a password, an SSH private key is used to authenticate:

```bash
ssh -i <private_key> <username>@<host> -p <port>
```
> **Note:** The SSH connection must be made from your local machine. Connecting to `localhost` from inside the Bandit server is blocked.

